{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22308 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Cannabisin-B appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a series of target relationships, with LoVo, HL-60, and Kadlongilactone A acting as intermediaries. These cells are targets of different compounds, including Decursitin B and Rehmaglutoside G, which in turn target DNA polymerase iota. The evidence suggests that Cannabisin-B may exert its effects by first engaging with LoVo or HL-60 cells, which then modulate the activity of the downstream targets. The consistent involvement of DNA polymerase iota across these pathways implies a potential role in the cellular processes affected by these compounds. The mechanism appears to involve a cascade of molecular interactions, where Cannabisin-B may influence the expression or activity of these targets, ultimately leading to the activation of DNA polymerase iota. This integrated pathway highlights the importance of these intermediaries in the biological response to Cannabisin-B.",
